'''Dríadas''' (Baliscano pronunciation: {{W|IPA|[ˈdɾiəðəs]}}; {{Langx|arn|Pikunmapu|4=northern land}}) is the second-most populous [[Regions of Balisca|region]] of [[Cerdanya]], within [[Balisca]]. It borders [[Cadaqués]] to east, [[Provence]] to the southwest, and the island region [[Arcadia]] sits directly north in the [[Strait of Ivorra]]. The region's name is derived from the colonial name for the [[Gran País del Sur|Ivorran forests]], "Dryades", which is derived from Aetolian [[W:Dryad|''dryad'']], or "wood nymph."

Originally dependent on [[Agriculture, forestry, and fishing in Balisca|agriculture, fishing]] and [[W:Trade|trade]], Dríadas pioneered [[W:Industrialization|industrialization]] in Balisca and was transformed into a manufacturing center during the {{W|Industrial Revolution}}. During the 20th century, its economy [[Cerdanyan Miracle|shifted from manufacturing to services]].

